      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "cpau:cc-e-1-tou-2026-07-01",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "cpau:cc-e-1-tou-2026-07-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 2 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) Sheet E-1-TOU-2 Section D.2 (SEASONAL RATE CHANGES) provides that when a billing period includes use in both the Summer and Winter periods, 'usage will be prorated based on the number of days in each seasonal period, and the Charges based on the applicable rates therein' (further discussion at CPAU Rule and Regulation 11, which is not in this corpus). The model carries both Seasons and all six seasonal commodity rates but nothing that allocates a straddling period's usage between them, so a consumer must supply the day-count split itself, and a consumer that instead assigns each metered interval to the season of its timestamp gets a different bill. urpx:prorationMethod (xsd:string, 0..1 on BillingModelShape) can carry the provision declaratively; it is used by no filing in this corpus, and the allocation arithmetic itself has no computable form in URPX v0.5.1. (2) Section A excludes Net Energy Metered customers (\"This Rate Schedule is not available to Net Energy Metered (NEM) customers and is provided at the sole discretion of CPAU\"). The model quotes the sentence in a description; cpau:e-1-tou-2026-07-01-er-residential-tou carries four ComparisonNodes (residential kind, single-family, separately metered, AMI) and no NEM predicate. Expressible: cpau:e-nse-1-2026-07-01-cn-nem-successor is a notEqualsOperator NEM test in this same corpus.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-06T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    },
    "urpx:ratePlanUniqueIdentifier": "E-1 TOU"
  },
  "urpx:hasRatePlanModifier": [
    {
      "@type": "urpx:RatePlanModifier",
      "@id": "cpau:e-hra",
      "urpx:name": "Electric Hydro Rate Adjuster",
      "urpx:initialEffectiveDate": "2023-01-01",
      "urpx:timezoneIdentifier": "America/Los_Angeles",
      "urpx:hasRatePlanModifierVersion": {
        "@type": "urpx:RatePlanModifierVersion",
        "@id": "cpau:e-hra-2023-01-01",
        "urpx:version": "2023-01-01",
        "urpx:changeReason": {
          "@id": "urpx:initial"
        },
        "urpx:modifierVersionNumber": "2023-01-01",
        "urpx:description": "A surcharge or discount applied to all CPAU electric rate schedules based on the strength of the City's hydrological generation portfolio. Applied to manage volatility in energy costs and the impact on customer rates. The adjustment value is determined annually in May (or when conditions warrant) by a 4x4 matrix of Hydro Stabilization Reserve level vs. projected hydro generation, and falls within the range ($0.066) credit to $0.048 surcharge per kWh. Applied upon Council approval.",
        "urpx:effectiveDateTime": "2023-01-01T00:00:00",
        "urpx:priceCurrency": "USD",
        "urpx:commodity": {
          "@id": "urpx:electricity"
        },
        "urpx:serviceRole": {
          "@id": "urpx:bundledServiceRole"
        },
        "urpx:applicableToRatePlan": [
          {
            "@id": "cpau:e-1"
          },
          {
            "@id": "cpau:e-1-tou"
          },
          {
